course: dictionary
lesson: 8778
title: Shaggy and what it describes
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Shaggy» describes hair, fur or threads that are long, thick and untidy. To work out which meaning fits, look at the words around it.
explain: «Manny the mammoth plods through the snow in shaggy fur, with small ears.» The snow and the plodding tell you Manny is in a cold place, so his fur is long and thick to keep him warm. Swap in "long and messy" and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Shaggy can also be a joke word. «A shaggy dog story» is a long tale that ends in something silly or pointless. Here the word has nothing to do with hair at all, so always check the whole sentence before you decide.
fact: Shaggy means having long, thick, untidy hair or fur.
fact: Shaggy can describe a carpet, rug or plant with long, rough threads or leaves.
fact: «A shaggy dog story» is a long joke or story with a silly or pointless ending.
fact: Shaggy coats keep animals like yaks and musk oxen warm in cold places.
fact: Shaggy is also the name of a character in Scooby-Doo.
exercise: Manny the mammoth walks through the snow in shaggy fur. What does shaggy mean here? | *Long, thick and untidy | Smooth and shiny | Wet and cold like ice | Short and neat
exercise: «Shaggy yaks with big hearts and lungs» live high in the mountains. Why is a shaggy coat useful for a yak? | It makes the yak look like a rug | It hides the yak from the sun | *It keeps the yak warm in cold places | It helps the yak swim fast
exercise: Which of these is a shaggy dog story? | *A long joke with a silly, pointless ending | A map of a park | A short poem about a dog | A list of pet names
test: «The rug in the hall was shaggy and soft under my toes.» What does shaggy describe here? | *A rug with long, rough threads | A rug with a smooth, shiny top | A rug that is hot to touch | A rug full of crumbs
test: Shaggy is the name of a famous cartoon character. In which show does Shaggy appear? | Ice Age | *Scooby-Doo | Finding Nemo | Peppa Pig
exam: Which word best sums up shaggy? | Very cold and wet | Loud and noisy | *Long, thick and untidy | Tiny and neat
